<title>USA: U.S. supply/demand soybean product estimates--USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. supply/demand soybean product estimates--USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA supply/demand soybean</p>
<p>product estimates (Oil in million bls, Meal in 1,000 short tons):</p>
<p>    Soybean Oil ----- 1996/97		 1995/96</p>
<p>    -		10/01/96  09/01/96  10/01/96  09/01/96</p>
<p> Beginning Stocks   2,010   2,010	 1,137   1,137</p>
<p> Production	  15,400  15,175	15,263  15,288</p>
<p> Total Supply	17,485  17,260	16,500  16,535</p>
<p> Domestic Use	13,550  13,550	13,450  13,450</p>
<p> Exports		1,700   1,650	 1,040   1,075</p>
<p> Total Use	   15,250  15,200	14,490  14,525</p>
<p>     Soybean Meal ---- 1996/97		 1995/96</p>
<p>    -		10/01/96  09/01/96  10/01/96  09/01/96</p>
<p> Beginning Stocks     200     225	   223     223</p>
<p> Production	  32,685  32,185	32,557  32,572</p>
<p> Total Supply	32,975  32,500	32,860  32,875</p>
<p> Domestic Use	26,750  26,550	26,800  26,850</p>
<p> Exports		6,000   5,750	 5,860   5,800</p>
<p> Total Use	   32,750  32,300	32,660  32,650</p>
<p>    Soybean Meal ---- 1996/97		 1995/96</p>
<p>    -		10/01/96  09/01/96  10/01/96  09/01/96</p>
<p> Ending Stocks	 225	 200	  200     225</p>
<p> Average Price    225-245   245-265    236.00   235.00</p>
<p>Note-Soymeal Average Price in dollars/short ton, simple average of 48 pct, Decatur. Soyoil Average Price (cents/lb) is simple average of crude soyoil, Decatur. Total Supply includes imports. 1994/95 soyproduct production estimates are based on October year crush of 1,403 million bu. Soy products marketing seasons begin Oct 1.</p>
</text>
